        "original_id": "2dda167f-e032-5913-8a10-96c88eee1cea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Philip Skinner, Edgar Ray Killen, Philip Glass, Allen Shearer, James Chaney, Andrew Goodman, Michael Schwerner\n- Organizations: San Francisco Opera, Ku Klux Klan\n- Works: Appomattox, Middlemarch in Spring\n- Roles: Casaubon\n- Events: Freedom Summer\n\nFacts:\n- Edgar Ray Killen was born on January 17, 1925.\n- Edgar Ray Killen was a Ku Klux Klan organizer who planned and directed the murders of civil rights activists James Chaney, Andrew Goodman, and Michael Schwerner during Freedom Summer in 1964.\n- In 2007, Philip Skinner created the role of Edgar Ray Killen in the world premiere staging of Philip Glass's opera Appomattox by San Francisco Opera.\n- In 2015, Philip Skinner created the role of Casaubon in Allen Shearer's Middlemarch in Spring.",
